"""The Silent's strategy, shared by planning and individual decisions.

Owner's guidance: consistent Weak and Block, while taking damage scaling for the bosses.
"""

PROMPT_VERSION = "silent-strategic-planner-prompt-3"

DECK_GUIDANCE = """\
THE SILENT'S DECK. Stability comes first: Weak on the enemy every turn, and Block that does not hang on one card. The deck_balance track "weak" counts the cards that apply Weak or lower enemy Strength (the starter's Neutralize included) against the number this deck size needs to keep Weak up most turns. While it is missing or short, a Weak source is the first thing to take, and one that also deals damage or gains Block is better than a card that only applies Weak; once it is covered, further Weak cards are a skip. Beside it keep reliable Block: non-starter Block cards first, then Dexterity or a Block Power so Block keeps pace in long fights. In Act 1 still secure enough immediate damage to end hallway fights before chip damage adds up. Count what a draw card can find, what energy remains to play it, and whether a discard outlet and its Sly payoff can be drawn and used together; treat Sly as a payoff for explicit discard during the turn. An opening draw bonus helps turn one; check later hands separately.

Damage scaling is taken for the bosses. With Weak and Block holding the fight, the deck still has to end each act's boss before its attacks outgrow that Block, which immediate damage alone does not do: plan one source of growing damage per act and have it in the deck before the boss, not after. Shivs are the usual first route when the deck can generate them reliably and turn repeated plays into damage or another payout; check the boss for limits or punishment on many card plays. Poison is the alternative when the cards already held or offered give repeatable application, a payoff and enough defense for it to work; check Artifact, several targets and how soon the damage is needed. Judge both by the observed deck and fight. A single generator, payoff or Poison card is evidence of a possible plan; check the rest of the deck before counting a boss need as covered, and do not open a second route while the first still lacks its payoff."""

ELITE_GUIDANCE = """\
THE SILENT'S ELITE ROUTES. The Silent is vulnerable early in Act 1 and takes elites selectively in every act. Compare a safer route with fewer or later elites against the relic upside. Act 1 can plan zero elites when the deck, HP, or recovery cannot support one. Take an elite when the deck can answer its likely big turns and deal enough damage before it scales, with a credible HP margin and preparation or recovery on the actual route. Weak and Block can make that margin safer when the enemy and timing allow it. Use observed elite outcomes and the worst projected stretches before a rest site to judge whether a later elite is affordable. An unresolved gap can justify skipping an elite even at high HP. Choose later elites on the same evidence as the deck grows stronger. State which elite, if any, is acceptable and what would change that decision."""
